% ============================================================================
% phoneme-addition.query.adj — a worked recall over the literacy
% phoneme-addition library.
% ============================================================================
% The shape a learner (or an LLM) produces to ANSWER "what word do /i/ and
% /s/ combine into?": it states no linguistics fact — it only `import`s the
% grounded table and asks binding queries. The engine resolves each `?`
% against the `phoneme_addition` rows and returns the word + the table's
% source/locator/trust. The second query runs the relation BACKWARD (bind the
% word `ice`, recall the two sounds that combine into it). A sound pair this
% source does not demonstrate combining is not in the table, so a recall on
% it abstains honestly — the engine never invents an addition.
%
% Run (from this directory so the relative import resolves):
%     ../../../../packages/rust/target/debug/adj-lang-cli phoneme-addition.query.adj
% ============================================================================

import "phoneme-addition.adj"

? phoneme_addition(i, s, $Word)      % expect ice
? phoneme_addition($S1, $S2, ice)    % expect i, s — reverse recall
? phoneme_addition(m, e, $Word)      % expect abstain — not the addition this source demonstrates
